      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Panel Look",
      "excerpt": "The tight look moves INTO Spell UI's property editor and its properties, so the",
      "text": "this can be a `compact` modifer on `<ui-property-editor>` etc",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-10-30T02:07:25.862Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "its Compact class and about",
      "offset": 202,
      "edited": "2026-10-30T02:07:31.423Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-10-30T02:11:53.598Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  the tight look is now a <code>compact</code> modifier, not the default.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>&lt;ui-property-editor compact&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;ui-panel compact&gt;</code> for its bands;  in Spanish the shared <code>compacto</code></li>\n  <li>the Inspector and the theme editor set it;  a property editor without it looks as today</li>\n  <li>tests check both;  the density count runs on the compact example</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The plan still waits for your Accept;  its Update block says what changed.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "p-panel-look#field-3",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Panel Look",
      "excerpt": "The tight look moves INTO Spell UI's property editor and its properties, so the",
      "text": "Other program did it:  number of columns in the <property-group>, some things can be `columns=2`",
      "by": "owenoak",
